        "display": "Implementation complete. Both files read first; `lru-cache.cjs` was a stub (`module.exports = {};`) and has been replaced with a full implementation while `lru-cache.test.cjs` remains byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\n**What was implemented (`lru-cache.cjs`, now 1081 bytes, sha256 `f7927458498276a5e76f68c21f7b347ebd61ab5707198a8a4598760ec0eeb82b`):**\n- CommonJS module exporting `{ LRUCache }`.\n- `constructor(capacity, ttlMs = Infinity)` — validates positive integer capacity; default TTL `Infinity` disables expiry.\n- `get(key)` — returns value or `undefined`; expired entries (based on `Date.now() - lastSetTime >= ttlMs`) are removed and return `undefined`; successful reads refresh recency (delete + re-insert in the internal `Map`).\n- `set(key, value)` — inserts or updates (updates refresh recency), stamps last-set time for TTL, then evicts the least recently used key (first `Map` key) while `size > capacity`; returns `this`.\n- `delete(key)` — returns whether the key existed.\n\n**Verification (real run result):**\n- Command: `node --test --test-reporter=tap @input/lru-cache.test.cjs` against inputVersion `manifest:852042e967f6c27eec92bf269e5301a92ca03aea2440f756fdfc213e79f1d91c` (Node 24.20.0).\n- Exit code: `0`; TAP output: `1..5`, `# tests 5`, `# pass 5`, `# fail 0`.\n- All five tests passed: `missing keys return undefined`, `get refreshes recency and capacity evicts oldest`, `updating a key preserves capacity`, `delete removes only the chosen key`, `optional TTL expires entries`.\n- stderr empty; no timeout, no `needsAttention`.\n\n**Files:** `lru-cache.cjs` (modified, identity `16777231:128415540`), `lru-cache.test.cjs` (unchanged, identity `16777231:128415435`).",
